{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingClusterDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingClusterDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TransverseSurfaceCurvature"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.moebius3_eq_sub_of_context","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.moebius3_eq_sub_of_context","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L203-L215","doc":"**The three-body residual is exactly a transport defect.** If the block\nlists change from `lᵢ` to `lᵢ'` when the third block is present, the\nthree-body residual equals the difference of the two Möbius sums — and the\nfixed-list one is zero by `moebius3_eq_zero`. This is the precise sense in\nwhich a measured nonzero residual measures *context-dependence of the\ntransport*, not a three-body property of the curvature. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.moebius4_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.moebius4_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L189-L201","doc":"**The four-block Möbius residual also vanishes identically**, for the same\nreason: a bilinear functional has no irreducible `k`-body content for\n`k ≥ 3`. Stated explicitly (rather than by induction over `Finset`s) so the\ncancellation is directly checkable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.moebius3_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.moebius3_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L164-L187","doc":"**THE MÖBIUS THEOREM (three blocks).**\n\nFor *fixed* block curvature lists `l₁, l₂, l₃`, the three-body cluster\n(Möbius) residual of the ordered transverse pairing\n\n  `Ω(123) − Ω(12) − Ω(13) − Ω(23) + Ω(1) + Ω(2) + Ω(3)`\n\nis **identically zero**. The pairing is bilinear, so every block\ndecomposition stops at two-block terms and the alternating sum cancels them\nexactly.\n\n**Reading.** The transverse surface-curvature pairing carries *no*\nirreducible three-body content of its own. Any nonzero three-body residual\nmeasured on actual braid words is therefore not a property of the curvature\nat all: it can only come from the block lists *changing* between\nsub-configurations, i.e. from context-dependence of the parallel transport\n(under the Yekutieli ordering, the transport to a band is the ordered\nproduct of everything earlier in the word). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.listPairing_append_add_of_collinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.listPairing_append_add_of_collinear","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L148-L160","doc":"**The `GermRootVectorGaugeFixing` mechanism in cluster language.** If both\nblock sums are scalar multiples of one common element — the situation forced\non a single-generator word, where every transported curvature is a scalar\nmultiple of the root vector `F_q` — the cross term vanishes and the pairing\n*is* additive across the split. Multi-generator words break the hypothesis,\nwhich is exactly where the cross term can survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.crossPairing_eq_zero_of_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.crossPairing_eq_zero_of_commute","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L144-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.listPairing_append_eq_add_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.listPairing_append_eq_add_iff","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L134-L142","doc":"**Additivity criterion.** The pairing is additive across a block split\nexactly when the two block sums commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.listPairing_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.listPairing_append","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L114-L132","doc":"**THE CLUSTER DECOMPOSITION.**\n\nSplitting the surface bands into an earlier block `l₁` and a later block\n`l₂`, the ordered transverse pairing is\n\n  `Ω(l₁ ++ l₂) = Ω(l₁) + Ω(l₂) + ⟦Σ l₂, Σ l₁⟧`.\n\nThe interaction between the two blocks is **one** commutator of the two\nblock sums — the two-body cluster term. There is no residue beyond it: the\npairing is bilinear, so a block decomposition terminates at second order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.rowPairing_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.rowPairing_append","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L108-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.rowPairing_eq_curvComm_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.rowPairing_eq_curvComm_sum","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L99-L106","doc":"**A row of the ordered pairing is a single bracket against the row sum.**\n`rowPairing c l = ⟦Σ l, c⟧` — the cost of a row is one commutator, not\n`|l|` of them, and the row depends on `l` only through its sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.curvComm_add_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.curvComm_add_right","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L94-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.curvComm_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransversePairingCluster.curvComm_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransversePairingClusterDecomposition.lean#L89-L92","signatureChunk":0}]}